<!doctype html>
<html><head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<noscript><meta http-equiv="refresh" content="5"></noscript>
<title>Pair WhatsApp</title>
<style>body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:32rem;margin:4rem auto;padding:0 1rem}</style>
</head><body>
<h1>Pair WhatsApp</h1>
<p>Open WhatsApp on your phone &rarr; <em>Settings</em> &rarr; <em>Linked Devices</em> &rarr; <em>Link a Device</em>, then scan:</p>
<p><img src="/pair/qr.png" alt="WhatsApp pairing QR"></p>
<p><small>This page auto-refreshes every 5 seconds while the QR rotates, but not while a phone number is being typed below.</small></p>
<hr>
<p>Or pair without scanning: enter your phone number (country code first) and type the code into WhatsApp via <em>Link with phone number instead</em>.</p>
<form method="post" action="/pair/code">
<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">
<input type="text" name="phone" placeholder="+919876543210" inputmode="tel" required>
<button type="submit">Get pairing code</button>
</form>
<script>
// A full reload every 5 seconds would wipe a phone number being typed (and
// mint a new CSRF token under it), so the page reloads only while the phone
// field is empty and unfocused. The reload is what notices a finished pairing.
setInterval(function () {
  var phone = document.querySelector('input[name="phone"]');
  if (phone && (phone.value !== "" || document.activeElement === phone)) {
    return;
  }
  location.reload();
}, 5000);
</script>
</body></html>
